Result): string", ""}}, line=388, name="BenchmarkModule"}}}, ["cosmic.check"]={examples={}, file="lib/cosmic/check.tl", functions={{description=" Render any Lua value as a readable string using the Lua serializer.", is_local=true, line=9, name="render", params={{description="The value to render", name="v", param_type="any"}}, returns={{description="Human-readable representation", return_type="string"}}, signature="(v: any): string"}, {description=" Deep equality check for tables; == for everything else.", is_local=true, line=24, name="deep_eq", params={{description="First value", name="a", param_type="any"}, {description="Second value", name="b", param_type="any"}}, returns={{description="True when a and b are deeply equal", return_type="boolean"}}, signature="(a: any, b: any): boolean"}, {description=" Assert deep equality between actual and expected.\n Uses deep comparison for tables, == for all other types.\n Throws with a formatted message when the assertion fails.", is_local=true, line=52, name="eq", params={{description="The value produced by the code under test", name="actual", param_type="any"}, {description="The value it should equal", name="expected", param_type="any"}, {description="Optional label prepended to the failure message", name="label", param_type="string?"}}, returns={}, signature="(actual: any, expected: any, label?: string)"}, {description=" Assert that actual and expected are NOT equal.\n Uses deep comparison for tables, == for all other types.\n Throws with a formatted message when the assertion fails.", is_local=true, line=70, name="ne", params={{description="The value produced by the code under test", name="actual", param_type="any"}, {description="The value it should not equal", name="expected", param_type="any"}, {description="Optional label prepended to the failure message", name="label", param_type="string?"}}, returns={}, signature="(actual: any, expected: any, label?: string)"}, {description=" Assert that value is truthy (not nil and not false).\n Throws with a formatted message when the assertion fails.", is_local=true, line=86, name="ok", params={{description="The value to test for truthiness", name="value", param_type="any"}, {description="Optional label prepended to the failure message", name="label", param_type="string?"}}, returns={}, signature="(value: any, label?: string)"}, {description=" Assert that a (value, err) pair represents failure.\n Expects value to be nil and err to be a non-nil, non-empty string,\n matching the standard cosmic error-return convention.", is_local=true, line=103, name="err", params={{description="The first return value (expected to be nil)", name="value", param_type="any"}, {description="The second return value (expected to be a non-empty string)", name="e", param_type="string"}, {description="Optional label prepended to the failure message", name="label", param_type="string?"}}, returns={}, signature="(value: any, e: string, label?: string)"}, {description=" Report whether the enforcement lane is active.\n True when COSMIC_ENFORCE=1, which the privileged, unsandboxed CI lane\n (`bin/make enforce`) sets. In that mode a sandbox test that cannot\n exercise real enforcement must fail loudly rather than skip silently,\n since there is no outer sandbox left to blame.", is_local=true, line=124, name="enforcing", params={}, returns={{description="True when strict enforcement is required", return_type="boolean"}}, signature="(): boolean"}, {description=" Record that a sandbox test could not exercise real enforcement.\n Writes a machine-readable marker to stderr so the enforce-lane tripwire\n can see the skip (a silent `return` is indistinguishable from a pass).\n When `strict` is set and enforcement is required (COSMIC_ENFORCE=1) the\n skip is escalated to a hard failure — use `strict=true` only where the\n mechanism was probed *available* yet the operation was still blocked,\n which on the unsandboxed lane can only mean an outer sandbox is present.\n Callers still `return` after calling this; it does not exit the process.", is_local=true, line=138, name="skip", params={{description="Why enforcement could not run", name="reason", param_type="string"}, {description="Escalate to failure under COSMIC_ENFORCE=1", name="strict", param_type="boolean?"}}, returns={}, signature="(reason: string, strict?: boolean)"}, {description=" Record that a sandbox test actually exercised real enforcement.\n Writes a marker the enforce-lane tripwire counts to confirm the lane is\n not a silent no-op (every test skipping would otherwise look green).", is_local=true, line=150, name="enforced", params={{description="Short name of the mechanism that enforced", name="label", param_type="string"}}, returns={}, signature="(label: string)"}}, module_doc=" Assertion helpers for tests with auto-formatted failure messages.\n Functions in this module throw on failure (level 2) so the error points\n at the caller's line, not inside this module.", records={{fields={{"eq", "function(actual: any, expected: any, label?: string)", ""}, {"ne", "function(actual: any, expected: any, label?: string)", ""}, {"ok", "function(value: any, label?: string)", ""}, {"err", "function(value: any, e: string, label?: string)", ""}, {"enforcing", "function(): boolean", ""}, {"skip", "function(reason: string, strict?: boolean)", ""}, {"enforced", "function(label: string)", ""}}, line=154, name="CheckModule"}}}, ["cosmic.child"]={examples={{body="\n  local child = require(\"cosmic.child\")\n  local r = child.run({\"echo\", \"hello world\"}) as child.Result\n  io.write(r.stdout)\n  -- Output:\n  -- hello world\n", description=" Example_run demonstrates the one-shot run(): spawn, wait, and capture the\n structured Result (stdout, stderr, code/signal, ok) in a single call.", expected_output="hello world\n", line=7, name="Example_run"}, {body="\n  local child = require(\"cosmic.child\")\n  local r = child.run({\"cat\"}, {stdin = \"hello from stdin\"}) as child.Result\n  io.write(r.stdout)\n  -- Output:\n  -- hello from stdin\n", description=" Example_run_stdin demonstrates feeding stdin to a process.", expected_output="hello from stdin\n", line=16, name="Example_run_stdin"}, {body="\n  local child = require(\"cosmic.child\")\n  local r = child.run({\"sh\", \"-c\", \"exit 0\"}) as child.Result\n  print(\"exit code:\", r.code)\n  -- Output:\n  -- exit code:\t0\n", description=" Example_run_exit_code demonstrates inspecting the exit code.", expected_output="exit code:\t0\n", line=25, name="Example_run_exit_code"}, {body="\n  local child = require(\"cosmic.child\")\n  local h = child.spawn({\"sleep\", \"10\"}) as child.Handle\n  h:kill()\n  local r = h:wait() as child.Result\n  print(\"signal:\", r.signal)\n  -- Output:\n  -- signal:\t15\n", description=" Example_kill demonstrates killing a running child. kill() defaults to\n SIGTERM (signal 15); wait() then reports the terminating signal.", expected_output="signal:\t15\n", line=35, name="Example_kill"}, {body="\n  local child = require(\"cosmic.child\")\n  local h = child.spawn({\"sleep\", \"10\"}) as child.Handle\n  local r, err = h:wait(50)\n  print(r, err)\n  h:kill()\n  h:wait()\n  -- Output:\n  -- nil\ttimeout\n", description=" Example_wait_timeout demonstrates a bounded wait. wait(timeout_ms) returns\n nil, \"timeout\" if the child has not finished in time; the handle stays\n usable, so we kill and reap it afterwards.", expected_output="nil\ttimeout\n", line=48, name="Example_wait_timeout"}, {body="\n  local child = require(\"cosmic.child\")\n  local cfd = require(\"cosmic.fd\")\n\n  -- Create a pipe: p.reader and p.writer are cosmic.fd Handles.\n  local p, err = cfd.pipe()\n  assert(p, \"pipe failed: \" .. tostring(err))\n  local pp = p as cfd.Pipe\n\n  -- Spawn echo, redirecting its stdout into the write end of the pipe.\n  local h, serr = child.spawn({\"echo\", \"from pipe\"}, {stdout = pp.writer:fd()})\n  assert(h, \"spawn failed: \" .. tostring(serr))\n\n  -- Close the write end in the parent so the reader sees EOF when the child exits.\n  pp.writer:close()\n\n  -- Read all output from the read end.\n  local out = pp.reader:read()\n  pp.reader:close()\n\n  -- Wait for the child to exit.\n  local r = (h as child.Handle):wait() as child.Result\n\n  io.write(out)\n  print(\"exit:\", r.code)\n  -- Output:\n  -- from pipe\n  -- exit:\t0\n", description=" Key steps:\n   1. Create a pipe with cosmic.fd.pipe().\n   2. Pass the write end fd to spawn via opts.stdout.\n   3. Close the write end in the parent BEFORE reading — otherwise the\n      reader will block forever waiting for EOF.\n   4. Read from the read end until EOF.\n   5. Wait for the child.", expected_output="from pipe\n  -- exit:\t0\n", line=70, name="Example_run_pipe"}}, file="lib/cosmic/child/init.tl", functions={{description=" Normalize an env table to a list of \"KEY=VALUE\" strings.", is_local=true, line=69, name="normalize_env", params={}, returns={}, signature="(env: {string}): {string}"}, {description=" Checks if a path refers to a /zip/ virtual filesystem entry.", is_local=true, line=81, name="is_zip_path", params={}, returns={}, signature="(p: string): boolean"}, {description=" Prepares an executable fd from a /zip/ path for fexecve.", is_local=true, line=89, name="prepare_zip_exec", params={{description="Path starting with /zip/", name="zip_path", param_type="string"}}, returns={{description="| nil The file descriptor ready for fexecve", return_type="number"}, {description="Error message on failure", return_type="string"}}, signature="(zip_path: string): number | nil, string"}, {is_local=true, line=99, name="close_fds", params={}, returns={}, signature="(self: Handle)"}, {is_local=true, line=107, name="finish", params={}, returns={}, signature="(self: Handle, status: number): Result"}, {is_local=true, line=128, name="cleanup", params={}, returns={}, signature="(self: Handle)"}, {is_local=true, line=144, name="make_handle", params={}, returns={}, signature="(pid: number, st: childio.PumpState): Handle"}, {description=" Spawns a child process with I/O control. Uses fexecve for /zip/ paths.\n Returns a Handle on success. If the program cannot be executed, spawn\n itself fails with `nil, \"exec failed: ENOENT: ...\"` — the error surfaces\n here, not as a bogus exit code from a later wait().\n To spawn cosmic itself, use `rawget(arg, -1)` — NOT arg[0], which is\n the script path (/zip/main.lua), not the interpreter.", is_local=true, line=217, name="spawn", params={{description="Command and arguments", name="argv", param_type="{string}"}, {description="Spawn options", name="opts", param_type="Options?"}}, returns={{description="| nil, string? Process handle or nil + error", return_type="Handle"}}, signature="(argv: {string}, opts?: Options): Handle | nil, string"}, {is_local=true, line=241, name="fail", params={}, returns={}, signature="(msg: string): Handle, string"}, {is_local=true, line=250, name="new_pipe", params={}, returns={}, signature="(): number, number"}, {description=" One-shot spawn: run to completion and return the Result.", is_local=true, line=417, name="run", params={{description="Command and arguments", name="argv", param_type="{string}"}, {description="Spawn options", name="opts", param_type="Options?"}}, returns={{description="| nil, string? The Result, or nil + error", return_type="Result"}}, signature="(argv: {string}, opts?: Options): Result | nil, string"}, {is_local=false, line=147, name="handle:kill", params={}, returns={}, signature="(sig?: number): boolean, string"}, {is_local=false, line=158, name="handle:wait", params={}, returns={}, signature="(timeout_ms?: integer): Result | nil, string"}, {is_local=false, line=177, name="handle:try_wait", params={}, returns={}, signature="(): Result | nil, string"}, {is_local=false, line=193, name="handle:read", params={}, returns={}, signature="(size: integer): string | nil, string"}}, module_doc=" Child process management.\n\n The high-level spawn API. `spawn` starts a process and hands back a\n `Handle` you can `kill`, `wait` on (with an optional timeout), poll with\n `try_wait`, or stream from with `read`. `run` is the one-shot form that\n spawns, waits, and returns a structured `Result`. Low-level syscall\n passthroughs (fork/wait/kill/posix_spawn, the W* status helpers) live in\n `cosmic.proc`; this module builds the ergonomic layer on top.\n\n A Handle owns the child: `wait`/`run` reap it and cache the `Result`, so a\n second `wait` returns the same value instead of failing. An abandoned\n handle is not leaked — its `__gc`/`__close` metamethods SIGKILL and reap an\n un-waited child and close its pipes, so `local h <close> = spawn{...}` (or\n simply dropping the handle) never leaves a zombie.", records={{description=" Structured outcome of a finished child.\n Exactly one of `code`/`signal` is set: `code` when the child exited,\n `signal` when a signal killed it. `ok` is true only on a zero exit.", fields={{"code", "integer", ""}, {"signal", "integer", ""}, {"ok", "boolean", ""}, {"stdout", "string", ""}, {"stderr", "string", ""}}, line=22, name="Result"}, {description=" Handle for a spawned process.\n Fields prefixed `_` are internal bookkeeping; use the methods.", fields={{"pid", "integer", ""}, {"_st", "childio.PumpState", ""}, {"_result", "Result", ""}, {"_closed", "boolean", ""}, {"kill", "function(self: Handle, sig?: number): boolean, string", " Sends `sig` (default SIGTERM) to the child. Fails once the child has\n been reaped, since its pid may have been recycled."}, {"try_wait", "function(self: Handle): Result | nil, string", " Non-blocking reap: the cached/final Result if the child has finished,\n `nil, nil` while it is still running, or `nil, err` on a wait error."}, {"wait", "function(self: Handle, timeout_ms?: integer): Result | nil, string", " Runs the child to completion (feeding stdin, draining stdout+stderr) and\n returns its Result. With `timeout_ms`, returns `nil, \"timeout\"` if the\n child has not finished in time; the handle stays usable (wait again, or\n kill it). Idempotent: repeat calls return the same cached Result."}}, line=32, name="Handle"}, {description=" Options for spawning a process.\n stdout/stderr as numbers are raw fds dup2'd onto the child's fd 1/2 (the\n corresponding Result field is then \"\"). See Example_spawn_pipe.", fields={{"stdin", "string | number", ""}, {"stdout", "number", ""}, {"stderr", "number", ""}, {"env", "{string}", ""}, {"cwd", "string", ""}}, line=60, name="Options"}, {fields={{"spawn", "function(argv: {string}, opts?: Options): Handle | nil, string", ""}, {"run", "function(argv: {string}, opts?: Options): Result | nil, string", ""}, {"prepare_zip_exec", "function(zip_path: string): number | nil, string", ""}}, line=425, name="ChildModule"}}}, ["cosmic.child.io"]={examples={}, file="lib/cosmic/child/io.tl", functions={{is_local=true, line=39, name="now_ms", params={}, returns={}, signature="(): number"}, {is_local=true, line=49, name="set_nonblocking", params={}, returns={}, signature="(fd: number): boolean, string"}, {description=" Drive `state` forward: feed stdin while draining stdout/stderr, all in one\n poll loop so no direction can deadlock on a full pipe buffer. Returns\n `true` if `deadline_ms` (an absolute `now_ms()` value, or nil for no limit)\n elapsed before every stream finished — the child may still be running and\n the caller can resume by calling `pump` again with the same state. Returns\n `false` once stdin is fully sent and stdout/stderr have both hit EOF; each\n fd is closed and nilled in `state` as it completes.", is_local=true, line=67, name="pump", params={{description="shared, mutable I/O state", name="state", param_type="PumpState"}, {description="absolute monotonic-ms deadline, or nil", name="deadline_ms", param_type="number?"}}, returns={{description="timed_out", return_type="boolean"}}, signature="(state: PumpState, deadline_ms: number): boolean"}, {is_local=true, line=88, name="read_ready", params={}, returns={}, signature="(fd: number, buf: {string}, which: string)"}}, internal=true, module_doc=" Low-level child-process I/O primitives.\n\n Holds the poll-driven `pump` that concurrently feeds a child's stdin while\n draining its stdout and stderr. Doing all three in one poll loop is what\n keeps large I/O in any direction from deadlocking on a full pipe buffer.\n The pump is deadline-aware and resumable: `cosmic.child` drives it through\n a shared PumpState so a `wait(timeout_ms)` that expires can be resumed by a\n later call, and the partial output collected so far is never lost.", records={{description=" Mutable state threaded through `pump`. `cosmic.child` owns one per handle.\n Each fd field is nilled (and the fd closed) as that stream finishes, so a\n resumed pump only watches what is still live. `out`/`err_out` accumulate\n across calls; `stdin_off` records progress feeding `stdin_data`.", fields={{"stdout_fd", "number", ""}, {"stderr_fd", "number", ""}, {"stdin_fd", "number", ""}, {"stdin_data", "string", ""}, {"stdin_off", "integer", ""}, {"out", "{string}", ""}, {"err_out", "{string}", ""}, {"io_err", "string", ""}}, line=26, name="PumpState"}, {fields={{"PumpState", "PumpState", ""}, {"pump", "function(state: PumpState, deadline_ms: number): boolean", ""}, {"now_ms", "function(): number", ""}}, line=158, name="ChildIoModule"}}}, ["cosmic.cli.args"]={examples={}, file="lib/cosmic/cli/args.tl", functions={}, internal=true, module_doc=" CLI option definitions for cosmic.\n Shared by the dispatcher and tests to keep option lists in sync.", records={}}, ["cosmic.cli.help"]={examples={}, file="lib/cosmic/cli/help.tl", functions={{description=" Generate help text for cosmic CLI.", is_local=true, line=9, name="generate", params={}, returns={{description="The complete help text", return_type="string"}}, signature="(): string"}}, internal=true, module_doc=" Help text generation for cosmic CLI.\n Produces the complete --help output including static option descriptions\n and dynamic module list from embedded docs.", records={}}, ["cosmic.cli.instrument"]={examples={}, file="lib/cosmic/cli/instrument.tl", functions={{description=" Check whether instrumentation is enabled.\n Returns true when COSMIC_INSTRUMENTATION is \"1\" or \"true\".", is_local=true, line=33, name="is_enabled", params={}, returns={{return_type="boolean"}}, signature="(): boolean"}, {description=" Begin a new instrumentation span.\n Captures monotonic wall time and CPU usage at the start.", is_local=true, line=43, name="begin_span", params={{description="Operation name (e.g. \"test\", \"compile\", \"check-types\")", name="op", param_type="string"}, {description="File being operated on", name="file", param_type="string"}}, returns={{return_type="Span"}}, signature="(op: string, file: string): Span"}, {description=" Finish a span and emit instrumentation.\n When instrumentation is enabled, writes a key=value line to stderr\n and returns the line. When disabled, returns nil.", is_local=true, line=71, name="finish_span", params={{description="The span from begin()", name="span", param_type="Span"}, {description="The exit code of the operation", name="exit_code", param_type="integer"}}, returns={{description="The formatted line, or nil if disabled", return_type="string?"}}, signature="(span: Span, exit_code: integer): string"}, {description=" Parse a single instrumentation line.\n Returns nil if the line is not a valid cosmic: instrumentation line.", is_local=true, line=112, name="parse_line", params={{description="A line from stderr", name="line", param_type="string"}}, returns={{return_type="InstrumentData?"}}, signature="(line: string): InstrumentData"}, {description=" Parse multiple lines of stderr, extracting instrumentation data.", is_local=true, line=138, name="parse_lines", params={{description="Full stderr content", name="content", param_type="string"}}, returns={{return_type="{InstrumentData}"}}, signature="(content: string): {InstrumentData}"}}, internal=true, module_doc=" CL