urns true if closed.", is_local=false, line=58, name="handle:closed", params={}, returns={}, signature="(): boolean"}, {description=" Returns the underlying file descriptor, or -1 if closed.", is_local=false, line=63, name="handle:fd", params={}, returns={}, signature="(): number"}, {description=" Read up to size bytes. Returns nil with NO error on EOF (Lua\n convention: `while true do local chunk = h:read(n); if not chunk\n then break end ... end`), and nil WITH an error on failure —\n including EAGAIN on a nonblocking fd with no data, and EINTR when\n a signal interrupts the read (see the module header; not retried).\n If offset is provided, reads at that position (pread behavior).", is_local=false, line=73, name="handle:read", params={}, returns={}, signature="(size?: number, offset?: number): string | nil, string"}, {description=" Write data. Returns number of bytes written (which may be fewer\n than #data — callers writing everything must loop). On failure\n returns nil plus an error; EINTR is not retried (see module header).\n If offset is provided, writes at that position (pwrite behavior).", is_local=false, line=91, name="handle:write", params={}, returns={}, signature="(data: string, offset?: number): number | nil, string"}, {description=" Seek to position. whence: SEEK_SET (default), SEEK_CUR, SEEK_END.\n On failure returns nil plus an error; EINTR is not retried.", is_local=false, line=104, name="handle:seek", params={}, returns={}, signature="(offset: number, whence?: number): number | nil, string"}, {description=" Truncate to length (default 0).", is_local=false, line=116, name="handle:truncate", params={}, returns={}, signature="(length?: number): boolean, string"}, {description=" Flush data and metadata to disk.", is_local=false, line=128, name="handle:sync", params={}, returns={}, signature="(): boolean, string"}, {description=" Flush data to disk (but not necessarily metadata).", is_local=false, line=140, name="handle:datasync", params={}, returns={}, signature="(): boolean, string"}, {description=" Duplicate the handle.\n If newfd is provided, duplicates to that specific fd (dup2 behavior).\n flags can include O_CLOEXEC. lowest specifies minimum acceptable fd.", is_local=false, line=154, name="handle:dup", params={}, returns={}, signature="(newfd?: number, flags?: number, lowest?: number): Handle | nil, string"}, {description=" File control operations. cmd: F_GETFD, F_SETFD, F_GETFL, F_SETFL, F_SETLK, etc.", is_local=false, line=166, name="handle:fcntl", params={}, returns={}, signature="(cmd: number, arg?: number): number | nil, string"}, {is_local=false, line=197, name="p:close", params={}, returns={}, signature="(): boolean"}, {is_local=false, line=203, name="p:closed", params={}, returns={}, signature="(): boolean"}}, module_doc=" File descriptor I/O operations.\n Wraps low-level file descriptor operations from cosmo.unix.\n Supports Lua 5.4's to-be-closed via __close metamethod on Handle and Pipe.\n\n cosmic.fd has NO stderr, stdout, or stdin handles. For stream I/O use\n Lua's standard library directly:\n   io.stderr:write(\"error: \" .. msg .. \"\\n\")\n   io.stdout:write(data)\n\n For whole-file path-based operations use cosmic.fs: fs.read(path),\n fs.write(path, data), fs.truncate(path).\n\n EINTR posture: Handle read/write/seek do NOT retry automatically. When\n a signal interrupts the call, it returns nil plus an EINTR-tagged\n error; callers that install signal handlers detect it with\n `errno.name_of(err) == \"EINTR\"` and retry themselves. (Automatic\n retry is deferred to the signal-safety wave.)", records={{description=" File handle for I/O operations.\n Supports Lua 5.4's to-be-closed via __close metamethod.", fields={{"close", "function(self: Handle): boolean, string", ""}, {"closed", "function(self: Handle): boolean", ""}, {"fd", "function(self: Handle): number", ""}, {"read", "function(self: Handle, size?: number, offset?: number): string | nil, string", ""}, {"write", "function(self: Hand